From 8ead97433862802878b625c6edbde981ef1efc3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:04:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor: personality-indexed pedal law
 (launch ceiling / pull gain / hold / cap)

The driver's LongitudinalPersonality (cereal log.LongitudinalPersonality: 0=aggressive, 1=standard, 2=relaxed) now
scales the whole Hyundai comma-pedal law, so the feel dial is the master lever for driver-felt launch/merge response
instead of only the MPC follow gap / easing rate (drive 149: personality=aggressive yet every launch was ceiling-bound,
cmd/ceiling = 1.00 for the first 3 s; the launch ceiling and the 0.35 interceptor cap were personality-independent).

- New CarControlSP.personality (UInt8) on the capnp struct + the opendbc structs.py mirror (default standard, so a
  no-arg CarControlSP is never aggressive) -> the car controller reads it off CC_SP and threads it into the pedal law.
- gas_interceptor: one feel factor per tier (relaxed 0.85, standard 1.00, aggressive 1.20, clamped to 0.30 -> 0.35);
  the launch ceiling (LOW_SPEED_MAX_GAS_V_OFFSET: relaxed -0.02/-0.03, standard shipped, aggressive +0.04/+0.06), the
  cruise-pull gain (PEDAL_SCALE) and the hold feedforward (HOLD_CMD) all scale. STANDARD reproduces the shipped law
  bit-for-bit. MAX_INTERCEPTOR_GAS is NOT raised (0.35, panda ceiling A 1218/B 612 unchanged).
- The upward slew limit is deliberately NOT personality-scaled (the comfort jerk is the same for every tier).
- New test_gas_interceptor_personality.py and the extended test_gas_interceptor.py pins.

Offline only.
